B.cDb=s(["Light from the Sun takes about 8 minutes and 20 seconds to reach Earth.","There are more stars in the universe than grains of sand on all of Earth's beaches.","A day on Venus is longer than its year.","The Milky Way is about 100,000 light-years across and has 100 to 400 billion stars.","A neutron star is so dense that a teaspoon of it would weigh about a billion tonnes.","The Moon moves about 3.8 cm farther from Earth every year.","If you could fall into a black hole, tides would stretch you like spaghetti. Scientists call it spaghettification.","Earth spins at about 1,670 km/h at the equator, and orbits the Sun at about 107,000 km/h.","Gravity is the weakest of the four forces, yet it holds galaxies together.","Astronauts on the space station are not weightless because gravity is gone: they are in constant free fall around Earth.","The universe is about 13.8 billion years old and is still expanding.","Saturn is the only planet less dense than water.","On the Moon you could jump about six times higher than on Earth.","Most of the mass of a galaxy is dark matter that nobody has ever seen.","Jupiter's gravity is so strong it pulls comets and asteroids away from Earth.","A year on Neptune lasts 165 Earth years."],t.s)
